<%#
  One product card, shared by the home page's trending grid, the catalog, and
  the detail page's related row.

  Expected locals:
    product        — {id, name, category, priceAud, imageUrl}
    priceFormatter — an Intl.NumberFormat. Passed in rather than built here so
                     one formatter serves a whole grid: constructing it is the
                     expensive part, formatting with it is not.

  The card is a link to the product's page. The mockup's star rating stays
  absent — the feed carries none — and so does its add-to-cart button, which
  would invite a click that no cart can answer; that one returns with the cart
  iteration.
%>
<a href="/product/<%= product.id %>" class="group block">
  <article class="flex flex-col gap-2.5">
    <div class="h-48 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-tint">
      <%# The feed does not always carry a usable image; the tinted block
          stands in rather than a broken-image icon.

          The card is a single link wrapping image, category, name, and price.
          The image's alt computes into the link's accessible name, so including
          the product name there would repeat it. An empty alt is deliberate,
          signaling this is not a forgotten required attribute. %>
      <% if (product.imageUrl) { %>
        <img src="<%= product.imageUrl %>" alt="" loading="lazy"
          class="h-full w-full object-cover" />
      <% } %>
    </div>
    <% if (product.category) { %>
      <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">
        <%= product.category %>
      </span>
    <% } %>
    <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-accent"><%= product.name %></span>
    <span class="text-sm font-bold text-ink"><%= priceFormatter.format(product.priceAud) %></span>
  </article>
</a>
